%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tutorial Table_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 97b4510909976a64082e7c15b4b1356d, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 10054545956864
    m_Localized: Nice to see you, User. I am <b>NA1L</b>, your OS and Video Editing
      Assistant provided by Manasoft.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151168
    m_Localized: 'Struggling with video editing outsourcing?

      Don''t worry!
      I''ll walk you through it step-by-step. And don''t even think about skipping!'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151169
    m_Localized: "\"Next, we encourage you to visit <b>MSN</b> everyday to contribute
      to the traffic growth of Manasoft\u2019s flagship network.\n\n*This notification
      contains advertisements for Manasoft.\""
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151170
    m_Localized: "<b>Mana Scroll Network</b> provides <b>daily news updates</b>.
      \nIt\u2019s perfect for catching up on what happened overnight!\n\n*This notification
      contains advertisements for Manasoft."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151171
    m_Localized: "Now, let\u2019s click the [X] button to close."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151172
    m_Localized: According to your contract, your work will be managed through OwlLook.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151173
    m_Localized: Oh, look! A letter has just arrived! Click on <b>OwlLook</b> to
      launch the program.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151174
    m_Localized: You can check the details by clicking on the subject line in your
      inbox.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151175
    m_Localized: "Manasoft is currently offering free daily special effects for Worlds
      Movie Weaver to celebrate the new Holy Warrior. \nCheck your email for details!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151176
    m_Localized: Per the contract, one editing request will arrive each day. Don't
      forget to check in daily.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151177
    m_Localized: "All the files you need are in the attachments. \nOnce you're ready,
      click the files and let\u2019s get started on the commission."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151178
    m_Localized: 'Manasoft <b>Worlds Movie Weaver</b> is a customized workspace designed
      for creating videos. '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151179
    m_Localized: Here, users can freely bring any vision they imagine to life.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151180
    m_Localized: Let's get started with the walkthrough for <b>Worlds Movie Weaver.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151181
    m_Localized: The program is all set, so you can start editing now. Click <b>'Start
      Editing'</b> when you're ready.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151182
    m_Localized: "Don't panic\u2014<b>NA1L</b> is here with you! Let's take it one
      step at a time."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151183
    m_Localized: "This screen at the top is the <b>Timeline Viewer</b>. This is where
      you can preview the video you\u2019re creating."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151184
    m_Localized: "This is the <b>Timeline</b>. It\u2019s the panel where you construct
      your video. Everything about your video is decided right here."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151185
    m_Localized: From the center, the top half is for <b>Enemy Clips</b>, and the
      bottom half is for <b>Warrior Clips</b>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151186
    m_Localized: This is the <b>Library</b>, where all your clips and effects are
      stored.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151187
    m_Localized: "And finally\u2026 the <b>Video Clips</b>! These are the main ingredients
      of video production."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151188
    m_Localized: You can arrange them on the timeline to create the scene you want.
      Shall we try?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151189
    m_Localized: "What\u2019s displayed here is the <b>Enemy Attack</b>. \nIf you
      hover your mouse over an enemy attack clip, you can see the target area in
      the Viewer."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151190
    m_Localized: "As it stands, this would be a guaranteed hit... but a hero should
      be able to dodge it with flair, right? \nLet\u2019s create a scene where the
      Warrior pulls off a stylish evasion."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151191
    m_Localized: "You can find specific clips by checking the <b>filters</b> at the
      top of the Library. \n<b>Check 'Move'</b> to find the right clip."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151192
    m_Localized: <b>Drag and drop the Move block to the designated spot.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151193
    m_Localized: Once placed, click <b>'Reset Selection'</b> to clear the filter.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151194
    m_Localized: "Well done! \nYou can click a Move block to change its direction.
      \nLet\u2019s make the Warrior move upward. \n<b>Click to change the direction!</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151195
    m_Localized: Great! Now, <b>grab the cursor and drag it to the indicator</b>
      to see how the Warrior acts in the Viewer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151196
    m_Localized: The Holy Warrior safely dodged! You can direct their actions using
      clips this way.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151197
    m_Localized: But you can't just run away forever if you want a glorious victory.
      A true Hero needs to strike back!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151198
    m_Localized: 'Looking at the attachments, there are two types of weapons the
      Warrior can use:'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151199
    m_Localized: "There's the <b>Ranged Attack</b>, \nallowing you to hit the enemy
      consistently <b>regardless of where you are...</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151200
    m_Localized: 'and the <b>Melee Attack</b>, which is restricted to <b>the row
      right in front of the enemy. </b>

      It may be limited in range, but it
      deals significantly higher damage.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151201
    m_Localized: "Let\u2019s place a Ranged Attack clip first. <b>Click the checkbox
      to find one.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151202
    m_Localized: Ranged attacks work no matter where the Warrior is. <b>Place it
      in the designated spot.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151203
    m_Localized: "Uh-oh. According to my calculations, that wasn't exactly the best
      possible move. \nNo need to panic, though! Clip placements can be modified
      freely before the sequence begins."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151204
    m_Localized: "You <b>can adjust clip positions using drag-and-drop</b>, \nand
      a <b>simple right-click will cancel any placement.</b> \nGive it a try\u2014use
      these features to <b>fix the layout of your Ranged clips!</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151205
    m_Localized: "Next up: Melee Attacks. \nSince Melee only works from the very
      front, you\u2019ll need to step forward one space. \nLet\u2019s <b>reset your
      filters</b> and <b>check the 'Melee Attack' box</b> to find the right clip."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151206
    m_Localized: 'This clip combines Move and Attack. Just what we needed!

      <b>Place
      it here</b> and change the direction so the Warrior moves into melee range.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151207
    m_Localized: "Nicely done. \nHowever, if we stay like this, you\u2019re going
      to take a hit on the next turn. \nAnd honestly... that's just not a very good
      look for a Hero, is it? This is exactly when you need <b>'Guard'</b>."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151208
    m_Localized: Let's reset filters and <b>check the Guard box</b>.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151209
    m_Localized: This clip assumes a defensive stance <b>to nullify damage from the
      very next attack.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151210
    m_Localized: "<b>Let\u2019s place that Guard clip you found into the designated
      spot.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151211
    m_Localized: Now, <b>click the 'Move' icon</b> attached to the Guard and have
      our Warrior step down one space.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151212
    m_Localized: Perfect. Now that all clips are placed, <b>press the Play button
      to execute the scene.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151213
    m_Localized: "What a magnificent video! \nAs you can see, the Warrior moves exactly
      as you arranged the clips."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151214
    m_Localized: By repeating this process, you can easily create a video of the
      Warrior's victory right here in <b>Worlds Movie Weaver.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151215
    m_Localized: "But beware\u2014video length is limited! <b>If you exceed it, the
      program may crash.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151216
    m_Localized: "Now, let\u2019s move on to the next scene. \nWe\u2019re going to
      produce an even more impactful scene this time.\nGo ahead and reset your filters,
      then <b>click the 'Ranged Attack' checkbox.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151217
    m_Localized: <b>Drag the 'Move + Ranged Attack' combo clip to the spot.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151218
    m_Localized: "This is a <b>Charged Attack</b>; the longer the charge, <b>the
      more powerful it gets.</b> \n<b>But be careful\u2014taking damage will cancel
      the charge!</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151219
    m_Localized: Now that you mention it, an enemy attack is going to land exactly
      when the Ranged attack ends.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151220
    m_Localized: "Seems they\u2019ll need to move somewhere safe...\nSince we're
      at it, why don't we try a special effect? <b>Click the SFX tab.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151221
    m_Localized: "<b>Special Effects</b> are <b>unique abilities</b> that make your
      clips more diverse. \nThey are usually paid features, but we're having an event
      where you can try some for free!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151222
    m_Localized: 'At the moment, only the ''Haste'' effect is available. Let''s try
      this.

      <b>Drag and drop the Haste effect onto the Move clip.</b>'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151223
    m_Localized: <b>Click the Move clip</b> and set the arrow to the left so the
      Holy Warrior moves to the end of the board.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151224
    m_Localized: Haste doubles your movement distance. Now we can safely dodge and
      unleash that Charged Ranged attack!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151225
    m_Localized: 'But do you see the Memory usage? <b>Each effect takes up space.
      </b>

      And once you run out, you won''t be able to use any more effects!

'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151226
    m_Localized: Don't let that get you down! Movie Weaver provides its own optimization
      features to keep you moving.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151227
    m_Localized: <b>If you follow these conditions</b>, you can maximize your SFX
      usage within memory limits.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151228
    m_Localized: "Now that you\u2019ve mastered all the features of Worlds Movie
      Weaver, let\u2019s wrap up this video and finish off that enemy!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151229
    m_Localized: "First, let\u2019s unleash a powerful attack to finish off the enemy
      once and for all. \nReset your filter selection and <b>select the 'Melee Attack'
      filter.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151230
    m_Localized: Good job. Now <b>place the Melee Charge attack in the designated
      spot.</b>
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151231
    m_Localized: "It has the traits of both Melee and Charging: \n<b>it only works
      up close</b> and <b>it\u2019ll break if you take a hit mid-charge.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151232
    m_Localized: "To pull off a move like this, you\u2019ll need to get within striking
      distance. \n<b>Let\u2019s place a 'Move' clip with the 'Haste' effect applied
      to it,</b> so our Warrior can dash straight to the front line."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151233
    m_Localized: Excellent. Now our Warrior is all set to execute that Melee Charge
      without a hitch!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151234
    m_Localized: "With these clips in place, you\u2019re set to deal a total of 11
      damage. \nSince the enemy only has 7 HP left, this victory is practically in
      the bag!"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151235
    m_Localized: "Now, <b>hit the play button and let\u2019s run the scene.</b>"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151236
    m_Localized: What a stunning video! It really looks like our Hero is clearing
      a real dungeon.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151237
    m_Localized: You did a wonderful job. Completed videos are saved automatically
      and can be exported immediately.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10054550151238
    m_Localized: "That\u2019s all from me! Was I helpful?\n\nNow, please <b>click
      the 'Save and Export' button to output your file. </b>\nThis assistant will
      now shut down automatically."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157630835187712
    m_Localized: To start, why not check out the trending SNS, Flutter?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157793226055680
    m_Localized: "\"Click the Flutter icon to check the latest timeline! \nYou can
      see in real-time what\u2019s happening in the world and what people are saying
      about the Holy Warrior.\""
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157874771714048
    m_Localized: Keeping up with trends is a basic requirement for an editor. Now,
      click the X button to close it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157970762555392
    m_Localized: Oh, it's a scouting email from the Holy Warrior!
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157985153212416
    m_Localized: For your reference, you can easily distinguish between read and
      unread emails by their icon shapes and bold text.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8157987355222016
    m_Localized: Before you start working, there's one more important piece of news
      to check... Shall we click on the email above the Warrior's scouting email?
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8158194767749120
    m_Localized: Click on the video title field and enter a great title that suits
      this clip. Once the title is set, the video will be automatically saved to
      the system and can be exported right from here.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
